ui: After waits while the window is occluded

Context.After asked for a frame built anew after d whether or not any of
the window showed, while animations and Painter.After already waited for
SurfaceShown (engine.next). An app whose view keeps a clock or a progress
current with After went on building its view while hidden, minimized or
covered, as an app closed to the menu bar: work and wake-ups nobody sees.

armTimer now leaves the host's timer off while the window is occluded and
records that a frame waits (afterHeld); SurfaceShown asks for the frame at
once. Changes of the state (Changed, Window.Update) still build frames
while occluded, as before; a timer armed while the window showed may fire
once after it hides. Backends without an OccludableSurface (Linux,
Windows) are unchanged.

Tester.SetOccluded(bool) hides and shows a Tester's window, sending
SurfaceShown, so apps can test what their views do meanwhile.

Tests: TestAfterWaitsWhileOccluded, TestShownWithoutAfter.

